KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [dcl.spec.auto]/3 + [temp.variadic]/5.  A decltype(auto) function
whose body declares a LOCAL type alias and uses it to construct the argument of a
nested deduced-return call (`using Ind = seq<0,1>; return inner(Ind{});`) -- the
shape of std::apply's `using _Indices = ...; return __apply_impl(..., _Indices{});`.
The local alias is not resolved during the eager return-type deduction, so the
return type stays an unresolved `<<type:decltype>>` ("invalid implicit conversion
from 'signed int' to '<<type:decltype>>'"), and here it even reaches
goto-conversion which aborts on the unresolved return type -- so the
desired-behaviour desc above (VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL / EXIT=0 / SIGNAL=0) does
NOT match and this registers as a known bug.  Using the value INLINE
(`inner(seq<0,1>{})`, no local alias) is handled correctly.  This is the residual
cpp17_apply_basic blocker.  g++ runs r == 1; clang++ accepts.  Flip to CORE once
a local type alias is resolved during return-type deduction.
